---
import Layouts from "../layouts/layouts.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import tiger_pc from "../assets/Tiger/Tiger_pc_bgr.png";
---

<Layouts
  title="Mubashir Dawood | Software Engineer"
  description="Personal portfolio of Mubashir Dawood, a Software Engineer specializing in JavaScript, Go, and AI integration. Explore my projects and skills."
>
  <div id="hero">
    <section id="header">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow" data-hero-item>Software engineer</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title" data-hero-item>Hi, I'm Mubashir.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle" data-hero-item>
        I build AI-native backends and the web apps on top of them, from
        bank-statement parsers and accounting engines to RAG pipelines.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions" data-hero-item>
        <a href="#contact" class="hero-btn hero-btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="/projects" class="hero-btn hero-btn-secondary">View projects</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="hero-tiger-wrapper">
      <Image
        src={tiger_pc}
        alt="Tiger"
        class="hero-tiger-img"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="scroll-indicator">
      <div class="mouse"></div>
      <span class="scroll-text">Scroll</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="about-cta" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="about-heading">Let's work together</h2>
    <div class="about-text">
      <p>
        From optimizing complex data pipelines to scaling background workers, high-throughput
        APIs to crafting seamless progressive web apps. I help awesome people turn
        ambitious ideas into fast, reliable, and accessible digital infrastructure.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a href="/about" class="hero-btn hero-btn-secondary">About me</a>
  </section>

  <section id="current-focus" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="section-title">Current Focus</h2>
    <div class="current-focus-subtitle">
      <p>Projects I'm currently working on</p>
    </div>
    <div class="current-projects" data-reveal-stagger>
      <div
        class="current-project-card"
        id="project-1"
        data-wake="https://simple-books-jyn9.onrender.com/healthz"
      >
        <h3>Simple Books</h3>
        <p>
          An AI-native accounting web app built for South African accountants.
          It reads bank statements (PDF or CSV) from all the major SA banks,
          categorises each transaction with client rules, built-in SA rules and
          an AI fallback, then posts balanced double-entry journals through a
          VAT engine. From there it produces the general ledger, trial balance,
          invoices and VAT201 returns. Built with SvelteKit, TypeScript and
          Postgres, and deployed on Render.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://simple-books-jyn9.onrender.com/demo"
          target="_blank"
          class="project-link">Try the demo</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="current-project-card" id="project-2">
        <!-- <div class="current-project-card-image">
                    <Image src="" alt="Project Logo" loading="lazy"/>
                </div> -->
        <h3>Workout Dashboard</h3>
        <p>
          As a fitness enthusiast and someone who likes looking at data, I
          thought it would be cool to have a dashboard displaying all types of
          metrics. With that idea in mind, I decided on a web app using react
          for the front end and the Recharts library to display those metrics. I
          also added a chatbot via groq that analyses a users data via vector
          searching in the convex database.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/MubashirD04/Workout_Dashboard"
          target="_blank"
          class="project-link">GitHub</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Contact />
</Layouts>
